{"t":15790,"mark":"replied","screen":[" ▐▛███▛█   Claude Code v2.1.318","▝▜██████▀  Haiku 5.5 · Claude Ultra"," ▝▝   ▝▝   ~\\agent-box","","","❯ Write four short paragraphs about rivers. No tools.                                                                   ","","● Rivers are the planet's oldest roads. Long before people drew maps, water carved paths through rock, following the","  slope of the land toward the sea. Each one begins as a trickle from a spring, a melting glacier, or a rain-soaked","  hillside, then gathers tributaries until it becomes something that can carry soil, sand, and stone for hundreds or","  thousands of kilometers.","","  A river is always working, even when it looks calm. Its current lifts fine sediment and drops heavier grains where it","  slows, slowly reshaping the valley around it. Over centuries it cuts canyons, builds floodplains, and shifts its","  course across the land, leaving behind oxbow lakes where old bends were abandoned. The landscape it leaves is the","  record of that work.","","  Rivers have also shaped human life more than almost anything else. Cities were founded on their banks because they","  offered water, food, and a way to move goods. Fertile floodplains, renewed by seasonal floods, supported some of the","  first farming societies. Rivers marked borders, powered mills, and carried trade long before roads and railways","  existed.","","  The same qualities that make rivers valuable also make them fragile. Dams, pollution, and drained wetlands can change","  how water flows and what lives in it. Yet rivers have a remarkable capacity to recover when given room, and restoring","  a river often means giving it back the space to bend, flood, and rebuild itself.","","✻ Cogitated for 4s · done 22:41","","────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────","❯ ","────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────","  ⏸ manual mode on · ? for shortcuts                                                                               /rc","","","","","","","","","","","","",""],"cursor":[2,29]}
